# Save and resume: create with what the app has, add the rest later, submit when complete. Drafts live on
# the server, never on the phone. Every response says what is still missing.

@onboarding = http://localhost:5100
@image = /9j/4EFUTEFTIFRFU1QgSU1BR0X/2Q==

### 1. A partial create: 201 DRAFT, nextAction COMPLETE_DETAILS, missingFields listed.
# @name create
POST {{onboarding}}/v1/markets/MB/applications
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{$guid}}

{ "firstName": "Test", "lastName": "Tester" }

### 2. Submitting too early lists every missing field as a validation error.
POST {{onboarding}}/v1/markets/MB/applications/{{create.response.body.applicationId}}/submit
X-Application-Token: {{create.response.body.applicationToken}}

### 3. The rest arrives later (a tunnel, a day). An invalid identifier here would be 400 identifier.format.
PATCH {{onboarding}}/v1/markets/MB/applications/{{create.response.body.applicationId}}
X-Application-Token: {{create.response.body.applicationToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "dateOfBirth": "1990-01-01",
  "nationality": "XB",
  "countryOfResidence": "XB",
  "identifier": { "type": "NATIONAL_ID", "value": "9876543210987", "issuingCountry": "XB" },
  "email": "applicant@example.test",
  "phone": "+15550100100",
  "documents": [
    { "type": "PASSPORT", "image": "{{image}}" },
    { "type": "SELFIE", "image": "{{image}}" }
  ]
}

### 4. Accept the terms: nextAction becomes SUBMIT.
PATCH {{onboarding}}/v1/markets/MB/applications/{{create.response.body.applicationId}}
X-Application-Token: {{create.response.body.applicationToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "termsAccepted": true }

### 5. Submit: 200 with the final answer, or 202 with the current status if it takes longer than 8 s.
POST {{onboarding}}/v1/markets/MB/applications/{{create.response.body.applicationId}}/submit
X-Application-Token: {{create.response.body.applicationToken}}

### 6. After submit, details can't be changed: 409 application.notEditable.
PATCH {{onboarding}}/v1/markets/MB/applications/{{create.response.body.applicationId}}
X-Application-Token: {{create.response.body.applicationToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "other@example.test" }
